  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "Find the area of the smallest region bounded by the graphs of \\(y=|x|\\) and \\(x^2+y^2=4.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac\\pi4\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac{3\\pi}4\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\pi\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{3\\pi}2\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\pi\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The circle \\(x^2+y^2=4\\) has center at the origin and radius \\(2\\). The graph of \\(y=|x|\\) consists of the ray \\(y=x\\) for \\(x\\ge0\\) and the ray \\(y=-x\\) for \\(x\\le0\\). Each ray bisects an upper coordinate quadrant, since its points have equal horizontal and vertical distances from the origin. Thus the angle between the two rays is \\(90^\\circ\\).\n\nThese rays divide the disk into a \\(90^\\circ\\) sector and a \\(270^\\circ\\) sector. The smaller region therefore has area\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{360}\\pi(2)^2=\\pi.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\pi\\), choice C.",
